WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.120 --> 00:00:02.949
These are the solar power towers of southern
Spain.

00:00:02.949 --> 00:00:05.129
This is one of the sunniest parts of Europe,

00:00:05.129 --> 00:00:07.919
and these were two of the first solar towers
ever built.

00:00:07.919 --> 00:00:10.900
Almost 2,000 heliostats, movable mirrors,

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:13.990
constantly reflect the sun onto the towers,
heating up water into steam,

00:00:13.990 --> 00:00:16.070
and powering a turbine to generate electricity.

00:00:16.070 --> 00:00:17.470
And if you look online,

00:00:17.470 --> 00:00:20.470
you'll see quite a few documentaries who've
gotten a tour around there,

00:00:20.470 --> 00:00:22.430
who've been incredibly impressed by the technology,

00:00:22.430 --> 00:00:26.170
and who've been selling them as the future
of power generation.

00:00:26.170 --> 00:00:27.550
And these are impressive.

00:00:27.550 --> 00:00:28.630
Not just visually,

00:00:28.630 --> 00:00:32.360
the technology behind them is both very clever
and very simple:

00:00:32.360 --> 00:00:35.329
it's like bothering your teacher with the
sunlight reflection off your phone,

00:00:35.329 --> 00:00:38.899
just on a much, much bigger scale.

00:00:38.899 --> 00:00:40.280
But there is a catch.

00:00:40.280 --> 00:00:42.429
When these were built, Spain was in boom times,

00:00:42.429 --> 00:00:44.640
and heavily subsidising solar power.

00:00:44.640 --> 00:00:47.170
Investors loved it and piled in with their
own money,

00:00:47.170 --> 00:00:51.270
companies and researchers were happy to set
up all sorts of things like this,

00:00:51.270 --> 00:00:58.080
and suddenly the Spanish government had many
times the amount of solar power they'd planned for...

00:00:58.080 --> 00:01:00.380
and they had to subsidise all of it.

00:01:00.390 --> 00:01:03.390
And then the financial crash hit.

00:01:03.390 --> 00:01:05.260
The Spanish government cut subsidies.

00:01:05.260 --> 00:01:06.260
Not just for the future,

00:01:06.260 --> 00:01:07.840
not just for the plants that were under construction,

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:10.060
but even for the plants that were already
built

00:01:10.060 --> 00:01:12.840
and relying on those subsidies to balance the books.

00:01:12.840 --> 00:01:15.660
The industry got cold feet: Spain had altered
the deal,

00:01:15.660 --> 00:01:19.280
and all the solar companies could do was pray
they didn't alter it any further.

00:01:19.280 --> 00:01:21.120
Or go bankrupt, one of the two.

00:01:21.120 --> 00:01:23.360
This might still have been viable, maybe,

00:01:23.360 --> 00:01:24.890
with some more research and development,

00:01:24.890 --> 00:01:26.770
and that's what they were trying to do.

00:01:26.770 --> 00:01:28.060
But now, the cost of regular,

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:31.180
everyday solar panels is tumbling.

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:32.700
Not mirrors, not like this,

00:01:32.700 --> 00:01:36.040
just normal solar panels, the sort that you can fit to your house

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:38.460
or that get put out in massive fields as solar farms,

00:01:38.470 --> 00:01:40.550
converting sunlight directly to electricity.

00:01:40.550 --> 00:01:44.220
Whether the price of those panels is going
to keep falling

00:01:44.220 --> 00:01:46.700
depends on which team of researchers you believe,

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:49.830
but it's already cheaper than building a giant
tower,

00:01:49.830 --> 00:01:53.240
putting in either high pressure water or molten
salt for it to heat,

00:01:53.240 --> 00:01:57.390
and dealing with thousands of moving parts
that all have to line up and track the sun

00:01:57.390 --> 00:01:58.390
perfectly

00:01:58.390 --> 00:02:02.420
and which might, occasionally, cook a few
birds in mid-flight.

00:02:02.420 --> 00:02:07.030
Don't get me wrong, this is a great bit of
technology on paper.

00:02:07.030 --> 00:02:09.490
It combines renewable energy with storage:

00:02:09.490 --> 00:02:11.390
if you're heating up something like molten
salt,

00:02:11.390 --> 00:02:15.370
you can save that power for hours to get you
through the night.

00:02:15.370 --> 00:02:17.629
And there are other plants like it being built:

00:02:17.629 --> 00:02:20.530
there's one nearly completed in the Atacama
Desert in South America.

00:02:20.530 --> 00:02:22.090
But right now,

00:02:22.090 --> 00:02:23.090
this is expensive.

00:02:23.090 --> 00:02:24.090
It might not have been,

00:02:24.090 --> 00:02:25.310
if history had taken a different track,

00:02:25.310 --> 00:02:30.700
if research had poured into these instead
of regular solar panels: but as it is,

00:02:30.700 --> 00:02:32.879
the future probably isn't quite this bright.

